03:18.664 --> 03:20.999
What's this?

03:23.293 --> 03:25.045
I thought we were helping each other!

03:25.212 --> 03:26.380
FAIL

03:27.798 --> 03:30.426
Everyone's doing poorly on the test.

03:30.592 --> 03:32.886
The questions are too hard.

03:34.555 --> 03:37.224
It can't be helped. I'll give you a freebie.

03:37.391 --> 03:38.434
Really?

03:38.600 --> 03:41.270
I covered this in class.

03:41.437 --> 03:45.441
Translate what I'm about to say into German
and write it on the back.

03:45.649 --> 03:47.025
Question 1:

03:47.192 --> 03:48.944
"Rheumatoid arthritis."

03:49.194 --> 03:50.362
How should I know?

03:50.529 --> 03:52.990
Someone, tell him what "freebie" means!

03:53.198 --> 03:55.117
Question 2:

03:55.284 --> 03:57.369
"A man holding a banana while naked."

03:57.536 --> 03:59.788
What was he talking about in class?

03:59.955 --> 04:02.207
Is this really a German class?

04:02.541 --> 04:04.209
The last question.

04:06.837 --> 04:08.130
"James Thomas."

04:08.380 --> 04:09.423
A name?

04:09.590 --> 04:11.175
And it's obviously English!

04:11.341 --> 04:13.802
I can't deal with this anymore!

04:16.722 --> 04:17.973
This is terrible.

04:18.140 --> 04:19.433
We definitely failed.

04:19.600 --> 04:21.310
We have to make up for this somehow.

04:21.477 --> 04:24.855
Everyone, you all did very poorly.

04:25.022 --> 04:27.775
So if you get over 10 points, you pass,

04:27.941 --> 04:30.235
and if you get over 20, you get an A.

04:30.402 --> 04:31.445
Seriously?

04:31.612 --> 04:33.280
Great! I didn't think we'd do it!

04:33.447 --> 04:34.698
Right? That saved us!

04:34.865 --> 04:36.909
Yeah. Definitely!

04:40.704 --> 04:41.747
A retake?

04:41.914 --> 04:43.123
No!

04:45.417 --> 04:47.920
They're acting stupid again.

04:48.420 --> 04:52.257
Be passionate, my friends

04:52.424 --> 04:55.427
Shine bright with the sun

04:55.594 --> 04:59.014
Dive into the blue sky

04:59.181 --> 05:02.976
And let summer take it all

05:06.522 --> 05:09.983
GRAND BLUE DREAMING

05:17.157 --> 05:20.994
Be passionate, my friends

05:21.161 --> 05:24.248
Shine bright with the sun

05:24.414 --> 05:27.543
Dive into the blue sky

05:27.751 --> 05:31.713
And let summer take it all

05:31.964 --> 05:34.800
An expanding ocean of possibilities

05:34.967 --> 05:38.845
Summer is our amore

05:39.012 --> 05:42.516
We'll swear to the crystal clear sky

05:42.683 --> 05:45.644
Summer is in our hands

05:45.811 --> 05:49.731
Be passionate, my friends

05:49.898 --> 05:52.901
Shine bright with the sun

05:53.068 --> 05:56.363
Dive into the blue sky

05:56.572 --> 05:59.992
And let summer take it all

06:00.158 --> 06:04.162
With a cheerful heart

06:04.329 --> 06:07.165
Don't mess with me

06:07.332 --> 06:10.669
Keep going even if you fall

06:10.836 --> 06:14.548
And let summer take it all

06:19.261 --> 06:20.887
So how was the mixer?

06:21.054 --> 06:25.058
It was terrible Look at this photo.

06:25.225 --> 06:29.688
-They came dressed in costumes.
-We went all out! You should be grateful.

06:29.855 --> 06:32.107
You guys never disappoint.

06:32.441 --> 06:35.360
By the way, you said you wanted to join our club.

06:35.527 --> 06:37.321
Do you know what club this is?

06:37.487 --> 06:40.741
Diving, right?
I wanted to try it out.

06:40.907 --> 06:42.909
It's such a grown-up hobby.

06:43.076 --> 06:46.913
I'm interested in what's in the ocean and in colorful fish.

06:47.080 --> 06:48.123
Great.

06:48.290 --> 06:51.877
Going diving with college friends on a tropical island!

06:52.044 --> 06:53.920
It's like a drama on TV!

06:54.087 --> 06:56.506
Then you shouldn't join this club.

06:56.673 --> 06:58.634
Isn't this is a diving club?

06:59.468 --> 07:00.677
Just kidding.

07:00.844 --> 07:04.222
It's not that we never dive,
but I feel like we never dive.

07:04.389 --> 07:06.975
Hey, new member!
Your welcome party is starting!

07:07.142 --> 07:08.185
Okay!

07:08.352 --> 07:10.937
Well, introduce yourself.

07:13.023 --> 07:15.692
I'm Aina Yoshiwara, a freshman from OWU!

07:17.819 --> 07:21.698
I'm interested in diving,
but I've never tried it before.

07:23.367 --> 07:25.702
Starting now, I want to learn lots and--

07:28.038 --> 07:29.748
Isn't this club weird?

07:29.915 --> 07:31.458
You took your clothes off!

07:31.625 --> 07:33.251
Don't be so surprised.

07:33.418 --> 07:36.004
You already got a good look
at the Izu Spring Festival.

07:36.171 --> 07:39.424
So you weren't just letting loose after the festival?

07:39.800 --> 07:40.967
What's wrong, Aina?

07:41.134 --> 07:42.177
Everything's wrong!

07:44.096 --> 07:45.472
It's nothing.

07:45.639 --> 07:48.684
But at least Kotegawa is supposed to be normal.

07:48.850 --> 07:51.853
Please, Kotegawa! You're the only one
who can set up a mixer!

07:52.020 --> 07:55.816
No, Chisa. I didn't mean I want you to sit on top of me.

07:55.982 --> 07:58.610
-Did you want me to step on you?
-Or not...

07:58.777 --> 08:00.737
What are you two doing?

08:00.904 --> 08:01.947
Nothing.

08:02.114 --> 08:03.156
Nanaka.

08:03.323 --> 08:06.410
Hey, Chisa-chan. Get off of Iori.

08:07.828 --> 08:10.330
Great! I'm glad there's someone normal here!

08:10.497 --> 08:11.998
Thank you.

08:12.165 --> 08:14.167
Nanaka, how about a drink?

08:14.334 --> 08:15.961
Thanks. Okay.

08:18.171 --> 08:19.214
I'll have this.

08:19.381 --> 08:21.591
Kotegawa was drinking that...

08:28.473 --> 08:29.474
Hey...

08:29.641 --> 08:30.642
Don't ask.

08:30.809 --> 08:33.395
You didn't see anything. Got that?

08:33.562 --> 08:35.939
Hey, you guys!

08:36.106 --> 08:39.735
You have to give a toast!

08:39.901 --> 08:41.153
Hold on--

08:41.319 --> 08:42.904
Yoshiwara...

08:43.071 --> 08:44.114
Yes?

08:44.281 --> 08:45.907
Are you interested in diving?

08:46.074 --> 08:47.993
Yeah. I guess.

08:48.160 --> 08:50.203
-Why?
-No...

08:50.370 --> 08:52.247
It's nothing...

08:53.248 --> 08:55.500
I was just glad.

08:56.209 --> 08:57.419
Right.

08:57.586 --> 09:01.256
You're the only person who joined
because you were interested.

09:02.841 --> 09:06.762
So, what equipment do I need to get for diving?

09:06.928 --> 09:08.138
Well...

09:08.305 --> 09:09.890
There's a lot.

09:10.056 --> 09:12.434
Just renting is fine in the beginning.

09:12.601 --> 09:14.728
For starters, a towel and swimsuit.

09:14.895 --> 09:16.813
A swimsuit?

09:16.980 --> 09:18.273
You don't like swimsuits?

09:18.440 --> 09:21.818
It's not that I don't like them.
It's just embarrassing...

09:21.985 --> 09:23.320
You'll be fine!

09:23.487 --> 09:26.072
There's nothing embarrassing about it.

09:26.239 --> 09:29.576
That's because you are all used to diving.

09:29.743 --> 09:30.827
For normal people--

09:31.620 --> 09:33.747
Yeah! Yeah!

09:33.914 --> 09:36.041
There's no one normal here!

09:37.083 --> 09:38.376
Are you okay?

09:38.543 --> 09:41.838
Anyway, today is my welcome party!

09:42.005 --> 09:44.299
So, everyone, put your clothes on!

09:47.719 --> 09:48.762
What's wrong?

09:48.929 --> 09:50.096
We're out of booze.

09:50.889 --> 09:52.140
Not even one bottle left?

09:52.307 --> 09:53.683
I estimated wrong.

09:53.850 --> 09:56.144
No way. You're a veteran.

09:56.311 --> 09:57.979
Then I'll go buy some.

09:58.146 --> 10:00.565
It's going to be heavy. We'll go.

10:00.732 --> 10:03.276
It's okay, the store's really close.

10:03.443 --> 10:05.028
Then I'll go too.

10:05.779 --> 10:06.947
I'm going now!

10:07.113 --> 10:08.532
Okay!

10:09.241 --> 10:11.284
Make sure you put on your clothes.

10:12.035 --> 10:13.286
Okay.

10:14.287 --> 10:15.997
She better get used to this soon.

10:16.164 --> 10:17.290
Yeah.

10:17.457 --> 10:19.835
Though, you two got used to this way too soon.

10:20.001 --> 10:24.798
Hey, who bought the bamboo shoots
instead of the mushrooms?

10:25.924 --> 10:27.384
What are you talking about?

10:27.551 --> 10:29.344
The bamboo shoots are better.

10:29.511 --> 10:31.221
You're kidding me.

10:31.388 --> 10:34.182
Bamboo shoots are for people with no sense of taste.

10:34.349 --> 10:35.642
No, no!

10:35.809 --> 10:37.727
Mushrooms are for people with bad taste!

10:37.894 --> 10:39.354
Hey! What did you just say?

10:39.521 --> 10:42.607
You can't even tell the difference
between a cracker and a cookie!

10:42.774 --> 10:45.569
Haven't you ever compared their sales?

10:45.735 --> 10:49.197
You bastard! This means war!

10:49.364 --> 10:51.324
Want to fight?

10:51.491 --> 10:53.743
Hey, wait. Stop fighting!

10:53.910 --> 10:54.995
-But!
-But!

10:55.161 --> 10:58.373
I thought I already told you,
you should solve things with a game.

10:58.540 --> 10:59.583
All right.

10:59.749 --> 11:02.127
What should we play?

11:02.294 --> 11:03.420
Well...

11:03.587 --> 11:04.921
Let's use a Ghost Leg.

11:05.088 --> 11:07.883
Tokki, Bukki, think of some games.

11:08.049 --> 11:09.968
Okay. Have you picked one?

11:10.135 --> 11:11.177
Yeah.

11:11.344 --> 11:12.888
And the result is...

11:13.054 --> 11:14.723
The Pocky game.

11:14.890 --> 11:17.350
-What in the world?
-What in the world?

11:17.934 --> 11:19.895
Hold on!

11:20.061 --> 11:22.105
Who's idea was this?

11:23.899 --> 11:25.275
Azusa!

11:25.442 --> 11:27.152
This is your chance.

11:27.319 --> 11:30.655
You guys settle this with a Pocky game!

11:30.822 --> 11:31.865
No, no, no!

11:32.032 --> 11:33.199
This is wrong!

11:33.366 --> 11:35.327
There's nothing wrong!

11:35.493 --> 11:38.538
It's the result of the sacred Ghost Leg. Just accept it.

11:38.705 --> 11:40.123
We don't have any Pocky.

11:40.290 --> 11:42.000
So we can't play.

11:43.043 --> 11:44.544
You're right.

11:44.711 --> 11:46.379
Then let's use this.

11:49.466 --> 11:51.801
It's kind of big, but it'll work.

11:51.968 --> 11:54.304
The first person who takes their mouth off loses.

11:54.471 --> 11:56.765
Ready, set, go!

12:00.268 --> 12:02.520
This looks worse than I imagined.

12:02.687 --> 12:05.357
We can't let Chii-chan and Aina see this.

12:07.442 --> 12:08.693
There's no winner.

12:08.860 --> 12:10.737
A tie? Too bad.

12:10.946 --> 12:12.656
This is impossible.

12:12.822 --> 12:15.992
It's killing my mouth.

12:16.201 --> 12:17.869
Too bad.

12:18.036 --> 12:19.454
Azusa, what's your idea?

12:19.621 --> 12:21.748
I thought I'd get some Pocky.

12:24.209 --> 12:26.962
Azusa says buy some Pocky.

12:27.128 --> 12:28.171
Pocky?

12:28.338 --> 12:30.256
Sweets? That's weird.

12:30.423 --> 12:32.759
IORI AND KOHEI WANT TO PLAY THE POCKY GAME

12:34.052 --> 12:36.262
What happened while we've been gone?

12:36.471 --> 12:38.932
You guys are enjoying this, aren't you?

12:39.099 --> 12:42.227
Why don't you guys participate too?

12:42.394 --> 12:44.062
Well...

12:44.229 --> 12:45.355
I'm okay with that.

12:45.522 --> 12:46.940
I don't mind.

12:47.107 --> 12:49.526
How are we going to choose who plays who?

12:49.734 --> 12:51.194
Well...

12:51.361 --> 12:53.405
With Rock, Paper, Scissors or something.

12:53.571 --> 12:54.614
I see!

12:54.781 --> 12:55.824
That means...

12:55.991 --> 12:57.867
All right! I get it!

13:00.161 --> 13:01.204
We're back.

13:01.371 --> 13:03.164
We bought--

13:03.331 --> 13:07.669
Out! Safe! Yeah!

13:07.836 --> 13:09.421
Welcome back!

13:09.587 --> 13:11.673
Why do you always end up like this?

13:12.007 --> 13:14.342
Wait, Cakey! There's a good reason!

13:14.509 --> 13:18.930
We were just playing Rock, Paper, Scissors
to decide who plays the Pocky game!

13:19.097 --> 13:21.933
You don't have to strip
to play Rock, Paper, Scissors!

13:22.100 --> 13:25.687
-This is naked Rock, Paper, Scissors. We have to strip.
-That's right.

13:25.854 --> 13:29.065
Learn how to play Rock, Paper, Scissors
without stripping!

13:29.232 --> 13:31.860
In other words, like normal?

13:32.027 --> 13:34.904
This is normal.

13:35.697 --> 13:36.948
Anyway...

13:37.449 --> 13:42.078
We got more new members,
so it's time to get ready for the license class.

13:42.245 --> 13:43.705
You're right.

13:44.914 --> 13:45.957
License?

13:46.332 --> 13:47.584
For who can strip fastest?

13:47.751 --> 13:49.461
It's for who drinks fastest.

13:49.669 --> 13:51.171
Why do you think that?

13:51.337 --> 13:52.964
It's for diving, of course.

13:53.923 --> 13:54.966
-Diving?
-Diving?

13:57.260 --> 14:00.305
No way!

14:00.472 --> 14:03.016
Is it our fault they're acting like that?

14:03.183 --> 14:04.976
I think it's half-half.

14:05.185 --> 14:06.644
I have to ask you...

14:06.811 --> 14:09.731
You looked at the textbook, right?

14:09.939 --> 14:11.399
Of course.

14:11.566 --> 14:12.734
No need to ask.

14:14.235 --> 14:16.488
They haven't looked at it.

14:16.654 --> 14:19.449
Let's give them a quiz.

14:19.949 --> 14:22.744
Do you guys know the hand signals?

14:22.911 --> 14:26.206
-Yes.
-They're gestures, right?

14:26.372 --> 14:29.751
They're important signals
for communicating underwater.

14:30.126 --> 14:32.879
I'm going to do them right now.

14:33.046 --> 14:36.257
Watch, and think about what I'm trying to say.

14:39.636 --> 14:41.513
Stop.

14:41.679 --> 14:43.515
Look this way.

14:43.681 --> 14:44.766
I'm going to dive.

14:46.142 --> 14:48.186
In other words...

14:49.979 --> 14:51.564
Stop right there.

14:51.731 --> 14:53.316
I'm...

14:53.483 --> 14:55.026
going to kill you.

14:55.401 --> 14:59.030
Okay, Iori. What are you supposed to do next?

15:00.156 --> 15:02.742
I'm going to shoot him first with an underwater gun.

15:02.909 --> 15:04.494
What's going on?

15:04.661 --> 15:08.039
We can't use hand signals with Iori.

15:08.248 --> 15:10.041
It's Kohei's turn next.

15:10.208 --> 15:13.044
You'll see how much better I am than Kitahara.

15:13.211 --> 15:14.546
Keep your mouth shut, dimwit.

15:15.421 --> 15:16.798
A problem has occurred.

15:17.674 --> 15:18.800
"Yahoo"?

15:19.717 --> 15:21.052
No more air.

15:21.928 --> 15:23.054
"Aiin"?

15:23.972 --> 15:25.306
I'm going to go up.

15:26.266 --> 15:27.308
"Yeah, yeah."

15:27.517 --> 15:28.852
How was it, Kohei?

15:29.018 --> 15:31.312
I'm going to watch over you!

15:31.521 --> 15:33.398
What a bizarre idea.

15:33.565 --> 15:35.817
You didn't study after all.

15:36.025 --> 15:37.068
-Sorry.
-Sorry.

15:37.235 --> 15:39.612
Well, I already knew that.

15:39.779 --> 15:40.822
Anyway...

15:41.281 --> 15:43.074
Try studying a bit.

15:43.283 --> 15:44.325
Now?

15:44.492 --> 15:47.620
Something good might happen once you memorize it.

15:53.668 --> 15:56.171
Iori, are you studying for your license?

15:56.337 --> 15:58.798
Yes. Just the hand signals, though.

15:59.716 --> 16:00.717
Let me see.

16:04.679 --> 16:06.556
This feels like...

16:06.723 --> 16:08.975
You should memorize these first.

16:09.184 --> 16:11.978
Good things really do happen.

16:12.187 --> 16:14.981
Hand signals are wonderful!

16:15.190 --> 16:17.525
Oh, by the way, Iori...

16:17.692 --> 16:19.110
Yes?

16:19.277 --> 16:21.988
I heard something just now.

16:22.155 --> 16:23.239
Know anything about it?

16:23.406 --> 16:24.490
What do you mean?

16:25.200 --> 16:28.995
I heard that you're going out with Chisa-chan.

16:30.914 --> 16:33.082
Oh, the signals are coming in handy!

16:33.249 --> 16:35.919
That signal means "a problem has occurred."

16:36.085 --> 16:39.130
Yeah. It's an important signal.

16:39.923 --> 16:41.132
What's wrong?

16:41.299 --> 16:43.384
Azusa, it's an emergency.

16:43.843 --> 16:47.639
Nanaka heard about it.

16:47.889 --> 16:49.224
Can you do anything to help?

16:49.390 --> 16:51.351
Okay, leave it to me.

16:51.517 --> 16:54.395
You're the best, Azusa!
I can always count on you!

16:55.104 --> 16:56.856
What are you going to do?

16:57.023 --> 16:59.400
Don't worry about it.

16:59.567 --> 17:03.446
I'm just going to tell her
who you really like.

17:04.614 --> 17:08.159
Well, I do really love Chisa!

17:09.619 --> 17:13.665
You like digging your own grave.

17:14.165 --> 17:18.169
Iori...

17:18.378 --> 17:21.923
That one means "come here."

17:22.090 --> 17:24.759
Iori is learning them by using them.

17:24.926 --> 17:27.053
Don't let him beat you, Kohei.

17:27.262 --> 17:30.056
Nanaka, just now, that was--

17:30.265 --> 17:31.557
Good!

17:33.393 --> 17:37.438
It seemed like you guys weren't getting along recently,
so I was worried.

17:37.605 --> 17:40.984
But if that's what you say, everything's fine.

17:41.276 --> 17:42.986
Nanaka, are you okay with this?

17:43.444 --> 17:44.570
What?

17:44.737 --> 17:47.198
You know Chii-chan and Iori are...?

17:47.615 --> 17:49.117
It's a good thing, right?

17:49.284 --> 17:52.412
They get along so well
that they look like they're going out.

17:52.578 --> 17:55.206
What a convenient interpretation.

17:56.541 --> 18:00.211
What if they really were going out?

18:02.880 --> 18:04.465
I'm not really sure.

18:04.674 --> 18:06.676
Right?

18:06.843 --> 18:11.514
-Azusa's question makes no sense!
-No...

18:11.681 --> 18:12.724
No, that's not it.

18:13.766 --> 18:16.728
I mean I'm not really sure what I'd do.

18:16.936 --> 18:19.480
I might get killed someday.

18:20.023 --> 18:21.274
Don't worry!

18:21.441 --> 18:23.067
That would never happen!

18:23.234 --> 18:26.446
Right. They haven't been getting along recently.

18:26.613 --> 18:30.742
Since I'm her older sister, I can't just ignore it.

18:31.367 --> 18:35.079
Then let's do this for tomorrow's practice.

18:37.540 --> 18:41.252
Okay. We're going to have you dive in pairs today.

18:41.461 --> 18:44.005
What? This is awkward.

18:44.255 --> 18:47.008
Let's change into swimsuits first.

18:48.301 --> 18:49.761
Let's change.

18:49.927 --> 18:51.179
You're changing here?

18:51.346 --> 18:53.514
Why do you care now?

18:53.681 --> 18:55.266
That's not what I'm talking about.

18:56.851 --> 18:58.770
What are you two doing?

18:59.854 --> 19:01.064
We're changing.

19:01.230 --> 19:02.523
In front of other people?

19:03.649 --> 19:06.194
Kotegawa, say something!

19:06.361 --> 19:08.529
We have swimsuits on already.
It's no big deal.

19:08.738 --> 19:09.864
That's right.

19:10.031 --> 19:12.283
Yours looks like underwear.

19:12.492 --> 19:14.911
Blushing because of your bathing suit?
So innocent.

19:15.078 --> 19:16.287
Yup.

19:16.454 --> 19:20.041
You guys could act a little more innocent, you know.

19:20.208 --> 19:22.543
I've had enough of these people!

19:25.838 --> 19:26.923
Nanaka...

19:27.090 --> 19:28.800
What, Iori?

19:29.008 --> 19:31.677
Why is Chisa paired up with me?

19:31.844 --> 19:34.555
I wanted you guys to make up.

19:34.764 --> 19:36.599
It'll have the opposite effect.

19:36.766 --> 19:40.645
It'll be okay.
Chii-chan is easy when she's in the ocean.

19:40.812 --> 19:41.854
Right.

19:42.021 --> 19:45.566
If she heard that, she'd be mad.

19:51.739 --> 19:54.826
Okay, Iori, don't get far away from me.

19:55.785 --> 19:56.828
Okay.

19:56.994 --> 19:58.246
What's wrong, Iori?

19:58.413 --> 19:59.705
Are you nervous?

19:59.872 --> 20:00.915
No...

20:01.082 --> 20:04.293
We're just going to swim somewhere shallow today.

20:04.460 --> 20:07.922
If you're scared, don't push yourself.
Tell me if anything's wrong.

20:08.089 --> 20:10.591
Okay. Got it.

20:16.013 --> 20:17.473
Okay, I can do it.

20:17.890 --> 20:21.310
This isn't the time for jokes...

20:48.171 --> 20:51.090
Chisa's not mad.

20:51.257 --> 20:52.884
Instead, she's...

21:04.187 --> 21:06.147
Oh, right.

21:07.231 --> 21:10.151
She's just being serious.

21:17.617 --> 21:21.162
To make sure an accident doesn't happen.

21:22.580 --> 21:27.210
So that we can enjoy
being underwater.

21:32.423 --> 21:35.593
For me, since I'm scared of the water.

21:42.225 --> 21:44.644
That was really fun!

21:45.102 --> 21:46.687
It looks like you enjoyed it.

21:46.854 --> 21:47.855
Yes!

21:48.022 --> 21:49.398
Good.

21:52.735 --> 21:54.403
Did you have fun, Iori?

21:55.738 --> 21:57.406
Yeah. Of course.

22:02.119 --> 22:03.412
Good.

22:08.834 --> 22:11.420
-They made up.
-Yeah.

22:11.879 --> 22:13.422
Everything's okay now.

22:13.756 --> 22:17.844
Well, still, you really are Nanaka's little sister.

22:18.010 --> 22:19.053
What?

22:19.220 --> 22:21.180
I knew it when I saw you from behind.

22:21.764 --> 22:25.560
You have a spectacular ass.

22:27.019 --> 22:29.939
Die twenty thousand times!

22:32.024 --> 22:33.317
DEEP BLUE AL FINE
KAYA MIZUKI

22:33.609 --> 22:35.695
Here's your mic, Kitahara.

22:35.861 --> 22:39.865
Me, too...? All right, let's do this!

22:40.074 --> 22:43.411
-Yeah, sing your heart out.
-You guys seem to be having fun.

22:45.037 --> 22:51.043
A fairytale whispers
In a fake world

22:51.210 --> 22:56.966
Hiding in the complete darkness

22:57.133 --> 23:02.930
I reach for the forbidden fruit
In my last days

23:03.097 --> 23:09.228
Now I know the meaning of the song about hope

23:09.395 --> 23:14.483
A broken gear will never stop again

23:14.650 --> 23:22.074
Even if I were to lose everything
I'd still want you to know

23:22.241 --> 23:28.164
Trapped in the sky so far away
I'm praying with ripped off wings

23:28.372 --> 23:34.128
Because we span together
The vows of areppegio

23:34.295 --> 23:40.051
If life sparkles only to the beat
of the resonating stars

23:40.217 --> 23:43.054
I'll sacrifice everything

23:43.220 --> 23:47.600
Till death do us apart

23:47.808 --> 23:49.810
Cheers!

23:54.482 --> 23:57.109
Thank you!

24:02.323 --> 24:05.910
-We're going to have a tennis doubles match!
-Hold on!

24:06.077 --> 24:09.121
-You're not dressed as a girl this time.
-It's come to this.

24:09.288 --> 24:11.582
We have no choice.

24:12.667 --> 24:14.669
A knockout!

24:15.294 --> 24:16.921
NEXT EPISODE
"DOUBLES"
